ate (you own these): src/components/Books.jsx, src/components/Newsletter.jsx, src/components/Contact.jsx, and src/lib/books.js. behavior: Books section (id=\\\"books\\\") fetches published books from supabase table 'books' ordered by created_at; renders grid of book cards (cover 3:4 ratio, title, description 2-line clamp, format badge, price, action button); free books -> 'Download Free' linking to supabase.storage signed URL; paid -> 'Get This Book' button (placeholder alert('Checkout coming soon')); empty state 'New publications are coming soon'; only when isSupabaseConfigured is true, otherwise show placeholder cards/empty state message. Newsletter (id=\\\"newsletter\\\"): email input + 'Subscribe for Updates' button -> insert into supabase 'subscribers' table; client validation; success/error states, loading state. Contact (id=\\\"contact\\\"): fields Name, Email, Subject, Message -> insert into supabase 'contacts' table; client validation; success resets form; error handling. Both forms must degrade gracefully when supabase is null (show a friendly note that signup is disabled). src/lib/books.js: helper functions fetchBooks(), subscribeEmail(email), submitContact(payload) using the supabase client with proper error handling. Do NOT edit files owned by other agents (src/components/{Navbar,Hero,About,Offers,DownloadCTA,Footer}.jsx, supabase/schema.sql). Report files written and anything that needs attention.\"}, {\"role\": \"implementer\", \"task\": \"Create a SQL schema file for Supabase at supabase/schema.sql in the JCROWN DIGITALS project. Read SPEC.md sections 4 and 6 (Data Model + security). Tables to define: books (title, description, author default 'Jediah Akeredolu', cover_image, file_path, file_format default 'PDF', price real default 0, is_free bool, is_published bool, download_count int default 0, created_at, updated_at), subscribers (email TEXT UNIQUE, is_active bool default true, subscribed_at, unsubscribed_at), contacts (name, email, subject, message, is_read bool default false, created_at). Use UUID primary keys (gen_random_uuid() or default gen_random_uuid()). Enable Row Level Security: books read-only for anon (SELECT), no anon insert/update; subscribers INSERT by anon, SELECT only by service_role; contacts INSERT by anon, SELECT by service_role. Ground the schema in the SPEC data model exactly (section 6.2). Report the file written and table/RLS policies defined.\"}]}"
