      "content": "Sub-agent reports:\n\n## Implementer 1\nReview complete. I inspected the codebase read-only as required by my MODE. No files were modified.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Current state of the assigned column\n\nThe 6 components in my ownership do not exist yet — `src/components/` contains only `Logo.jsx` and `Reveal.jsx`. `src/App.jsx:1-9` imports all 9 sections already, so the build as-is would fail on module resolution. Each component needs to be created from scratch; everything needed to write them already exists.\n\n### 2. All tokens/copy needed are present — no gaps\n\n| Need | Source | Reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| `btn-gold`, `btn-ghost`, `eyebrow`, `gold-divider`, `container-x` | `src/index.css:39-57` | Ready to use directly in Tailwind classes |\n| `section[id]` anchor offset (88px) | `src/index.css:15-17` | Anchor jumps already offset for the fixed navbar |\n| `Logo` (default export) | `src/components/Logo.jsx:20` | `<Logo />` usable in navbar + footer |\n| `Reveal` (default, props `children/className/delay`) | `src/components/Reveal.jsx:7` | Wrap sections/items for fade-up |\n| `site` (name, owner, tagline, quote) | `src/lib/content.js:7-13` | Hero copy |\n| `about` (title, bio, portrait) | `src/lib/content.js:15-23` | About copy; note `portrait: null` — must render the null case gracefully |\n| `offers` (3 features with `icon` string) | `src/lib/content.js:25-49` | icon values: `book`, `gift`, `sparkles` |\n| `socials` | `src/lib/content.js:69-74` | Currently an **empty array** — footer must handle zero socials |\n| `lucide-react` | `package.json:14` | `book`, `gift`, `sparkles`, `chevron-down`, `menu`, `x` all available |\n| Theme colors | `tailwind.config.js:6-19` | `ink`, `charcoal`, `panel`, `gold`, `ivory`, `muted`, `line` |\n\n### 3. Concrete implementation plan / suggestions (for the build pass)\n\n**Navbar.jsx** — fixed 70px header (`h-[70px]` per SPEC 4), transparent over hero, switch to `bg-ink` + border/shadow when `window.scrollY > 10` (add/remove a class via `useEffect` scroll listener, or use a `scrolled` state). Left: `<Logo />`. Right (hidden on mobile): links `#about`, `#offers`, `#download`, `#books`, `#contact` with gold hover (`hover:text-gold`). Mobile: `menu`/`x` toggle + full-screen overlay of `bg-ink`. Imports from `lucide-react`: `menu`, `x` (and optionally `useEffect/useState` from react). No `#top` link needed — `Logo` already anchors to `#top`.\n\n**Hero.jsx** — `<section id=\"top\" className=\"relative flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-ink\">`; center column with `eyebrow` (\"JCROWN DIGITALS\" / wordmark), h1 serif quote from `site.quote`, welcome paragraph from `site.tagline`, and a `chevron-down` link to `#about` pinned at the bottom (`absolute bottom-8`). Use the `Logo` wordmark and/or `site.name`. Add a subtle gold radial/gradient overlay. `min-h-screen` already gives 100vh.\n\n**About.jsx** — `<section id=\"about\">` two-column on `md:` (40/60 split per SPEC 4): left portrait, right bio. Portrait: `about.portrait` is null, so render a fallback placeholder (e.g. a `panel` with the `CrownMark` or `Portrait` courtesy block) instead of a broken `img`. Use `gold-divider` vertically/gold capped divider between columns and an `eyebrow` + `font-display` title from `about.title`; map `about.bio` paragraphs.\n\n**Offers.jsx** — `<section id=\"offers\">` with `eyebrow` + `offers.title`/`offers.description`; `grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3` of feature cards. Each card: `bg-panel border border-line rounded` with hover lift + gold border glow — e.g. `transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-gold hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(201,168,76,0.15)]`. Icon: map `offers.features[i].icon` string → lucide component (`book`, `gift`, `sparkles`) in a small gold-dashed ring.\n\n**DownloadCTA.jsx** — `<section id=\"download\">` centered; a large gold button `btn-gold` with label **DOWNLOAD BOOKS HERE** (`<a href=\"#books\" className=\"btn-gold ...\">`). Keep `<a>` not `<button>` since it's an anchor (`#books`), or `btn-ghost` secondary link. Centered with generous `py-24/32`.\n\n**Footer.jsx** — `<footer className=\"bg-charcoal/40 border-t border-line\">`; brand `<Logo />` + `site.owner`, quick links to `#about/#offers/#books/#contact`, placeholder links \"Privacy Policy\" and \"Terms\" (SPEC 4 — likely `href=\"#\"` or `#top`), then `socials` from `content.js` — but `socials` is an **empty array**, so the footer must render nothing (or a fixed placeholder) for links rather than crashing; ` {new Date().getFullYear()} {site.name}`.\n\n### 4. Risks / edge cases to handle\n\n- `about.portrait` is null and `socials` is `[]` — both must render gracefully (no broken images, no empty link lists), or the implementer should add copy/placeholders in `content.js`.\n- `Navbar` scroll state — use a passive scroll listener and clean up in `useEffect` to avoid leaks; consider `prefers-reduced-motion` (already handled globally in CSS at `src/index.css:83-93`).\n- Specify `<a href=\"#books\">` for the CTA and `href=\"#about\"` for the hero chevron — the 88px scroll-margin in `index.css:16` handles offset.\n- No TypeScript, functional components only, default exports named to match the `App.jsx` imports (`Navbar`, `Hero`, `About`, `Offers`, `DownloadCTA`, `Footer`).\n\n### 5. Verification note\n\nI ran no commands (read-only mode). After building, verify with `npm install` (node_modules currently absent) then `npm run build`. All required dependencies (`react`, `lucide-react`) are already in `package.json:12-17`.\n\n**Decision taken:** the assigned task says \"build,\" but my MODE is Review — I did not create or modify files. I'm reporting the findings and a precise, ready-to-execute plan for the build pass.\n\n## Implementer 2\nYou're right that my replies keep hitting the length limit. Let me finish cleanly: complete the trailing snippet of `Contact.jsx`, then deliver the consolidated report. Since no write tool exists in this environment, I'll keep each code block short so nothing gets truncated.\n\n### Contact.jsx — final closing block (rest of error block + component close)\n\n```jsx\n   {status === 'error' && (\n     <p className=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-danger\" role=\"alert\">\n       {message}\n     </p>\n   )}\n   </form>\n   </Reveal>\n   )}\n   </div>\n     </section>\n   )\n }\n```\n\n### src/lib/books.js (complete file)\n\n```js\nimport { supabase } from './supabase.js'\n```\n\n```js\nconst BOOKS_BUCKET = 'book-files'\n\nfunction isRemoteUrl(path) {\n  return typeof path === 'string' && /^https?:\\/\\//i.test(path)\n}\n\nfunction toPublicUrl(path) {\n  if (!path) return null\n  if (isRemoteUrl(path)) return path\n  if (!supabase) return null\n  const { data } = supabase.storage.from(BOOKS_BUCKET).getPublicUrl(path)\n  return data?.publicUrl ?? null\n}\n\nasync function toSignedUrl(path, expiresIn = 3600) {\n  if (!path) return null\n  if (isRemoteUrl(path)) return path\n  if (!supabase) return null\n  const { data, error } = await supabase.storage\n    .from(BOOKS_BUCKET)\n    .createSignedUrl(path, expiresIn, { download: true })\n  if (error) return null\n  return data?.signedUrl ?? null\n}\n```\n\n```js\nexport async function fetchBooks() {\n  if (!supabase) return { books: [], error: null }\n\n  const { data, error } = await supabase\n    .from('books')\n    .select('*')\n    .eq('is_published', true)\n    .order('created_at', { ascending: false })\n\n  if (error) return { books: [], error }\n\n  const books = await Promise.all(\n    (data || []).map(async (row) => {\n      const isFree = Boolean(row.is_free)\n      return {\n        id: row.id,\n        title: row.title || 'Untitled publication',\n        description: row.description || '',\n        format: (row.file_format || row.format || 'PDF').toUpperCase(),\n        price: Number(row.price) || 0,\n        isFree,\n        coverUrl: toPublicUrl(row.cover_image || row.cover_url),\n        downloadUrl: isFree ? await toSignedUrl(row.file_path) : null,\n        createdAt: row.created_at,\n      }\n    })\n  )\n\n  return { books, error: null }\n}\n```\n\n```js\nexport async function subscribeEmail(email) {\n  if (!supabase) {\n    return { error: { message: 'Newsletter signup is currently disabled.' } }\n  }\n\n  const { data, error } = await supabase\n    .from('subscribers')\n    .insert({ email })\n    .select()\n\n  if (error) {\n    if (error.code === '23505') {\n      return { data, error: { message: \"You're already on the list — thanks!\" } }\n    }\n    return { data, error }\n  }\n\n  return { data, error }\n}\n\nexport async function submitContact(payload) {\n  if (!supabase) {\n    return { error: { message: 'The contact form is currently disabled.' } }\n  }\n\n  const { error } = await supabase.from('contacts').insert({\n    name: payload.name,\n    email: payload.email,\n    subject: payload.subject,\n    message: payload.message,\n  })\n\n  return { error }\n}\n```\n\nThat is the complete `src/lib/books.js`. Now the consolidated report.\n\n## Implementer 3\nI have all the information needed. Let me verify the SPEC section numbering to confirm 6.2 is the Data Model. SPEC section 6 is \"Technical Approach\", and within it the \"Data Model\" subsection appears at lines 226-269. Let me confirm whether it's labeled 6.2.\n\nLooking at SPEC.md: section 6 heading is \"Technical Approach\" (line 187), with subsections \"Stack\", \"API Design\", \"Data Model\", \"Authentication\", \"File Handling\", \"Security\". The Data Model subsection is the third subsection, likely 6.3, but the task labels it 6.2. Regardless, the task's instruction maps to \"Data Model + security\" which is what I'm grounding in (lines 226-292).\n\nNow I have everything. Per mode REVIEW, I do **not** write files. I'll report the concrete proposed `supabase/schema.sql` content, mapped to SPEC fields, with RLS policies, plus findings and issues.\n\nLet me compile the full report.\n\n## Review Findings\n\n### 1. No existing `supabase/` directory or `schema.sql`\n`list_dir(\"\")` shows no `supabase/` folder, and `search` for `schema` returns only PROGRESS.md mentions. The file must be created fresh at `supabase/schema.sql`.\n\n### 2. SPEC grounding (technical approach, section 6)\nThe SPEC defines three tables (SPEC.md:228-257) with these mapped columns:\n\n- **books** (SPEC.md:228-241): `title`, `description`, `author` (default \"Jediah Akeredolu\"), `cover_image`, `file_path`, `file_format`, `price` (REAL, 0 for free), `is_free`, `is_published`, `download_count` (default 0), `created_at`, `updated_at`\n- **subscribers** (SPEC.md:243-248): `email` (TEXT UNIQUE), `is_active` (default 1), `subscribed_at`, `unsubscribed_at`\n- **contacts** (SPEC.md:250-257): `name`, `email`, `subject`, `message`, `is_read` (default 0), `created_at`\n\nThe task's field list matches the SPEC exactly. Note the SPEC is the original SQLite model; the task adapts it to Supabase/Postgres (INTEGER booleans -> `bool`, INTEGER PK -> UUID, DATETIME -> timestamptz). This is the correct adaptation for Supabase.\n\n### 3. Proposed `supabase/schema.sql` (content to be written on approve)\nThe following is the exact content I would write:\n\n```sql\n-- ===\n-- JCROWN DIGITALS — Supabase Schema\n-- Grounded in SPEC.md section 6 \"Technical Approach\" (Data Model + Security)\n-- Run in: Supabase Dashboard -> SQL Editor\n-- ===\n\n-- books: admin-created publications (SPEC: books data model)\ncreate table if not exists public.books (\n  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),\n  title text not null,\n  description text,\n  author text not null default 'Jediah Akeredolu',\n  cover_image text,\n  file_path text,\n  file_format text not null default 'PDF',\n  price real not null default 0,\n  is_free boolean not null default false,\n  is_published boolean not null default false,\n  download_count integer not null default 0,\n  created_at timestamptz not null default now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz not null default now()\n);\n\n-- subscribers: newsletter signups (SPEC: subscribers data model)\ncreate table if not exists public.subscribers (\n  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),\n  email text unique not null,\n  is_active boolean not null default true,\n  subscribed_at timestamptz not null default now(),\n  unsubscribed_at timestamptz\n);\n\n-- contacts: contact-form messages (SPEC: contacts data model)\ncreate table if not exists public.contacts (\n  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),\n  name text not null,\n  email text not null,\n  subject text,\n  message text not null,\n  is_read boolean not null default false,\n  created_at timestamptz not null default now()\n);\n\n-- ===\n-- Row Level Security\n-- books: anon can read published books only; no anon writes\n-- ===\nalter table public.books enable row level security;\nalter table public.subscribers enable row level security;\nalter table public.contacts enable row level security;\n\n-- books: PUBLIC read (only published)\ndrop policy if exists \"books_select_published\" on public.books;\ncreate policy \"books_select_published\"\n  on public.books for select\n  to anon\n  using (is_published = true);\n\n-- books: block anon writes (RLS default-deny covers this when\n-- no insert/update policy exists for anon)\n\n-- subscribers: anon may INSERT; only service_role reads\ndrop policy if exists \"subscribers_insert\" on public.subscribers;\ncreate policy \"subscribers_insert\"\n  on public.subscribers for insert\n  to anon\n  with check (true);\n\ndrop policy if exists \"subscribers_select_service\" on public.subscribers;\ncreate policy \"subscribers_select_service\"\n  on public.subscribers for select\n  to service_role\n  using (true);\n\n-- contacts: anon may INSERT; only service_role reads\ndrop policy if exists \"contacts_insert\" on public.contacts;\ncreate policy \"contacts_insert\"\n  on public.contacts for insert\n  to anon\n  with check (true);\n\ndrop policy if exists \"contacts_select_service\" on public.contacts;\ncreate policy \"contacts_select_service\"\n  on public.contacts for select\n  to service_role\n  using (true);\n```\n\n### 4. RLS policy mapping to requirements\n| Requirement | Implementation | Policy |\n|---|---|---|\n| books: anon SELECT (published) | `to anon ... using (is_published = true)` | `books_select_published` |\n| books: no anon insert/update | No anon insert/update policy written; RLS default-deny when RLS enabled | (n/a) |\n| subscribers: anon INSERT | `to anon ... with check (true)` | `subscribers_insert` |\n| subscribers: SELECT only service_role | `to service_role ... using (true)` | `subscribers_select_service` |\n| contacts: anon INSERT | `to anon ... with check (true)` | `contacts_insert` |\n| contacts: SELECT only service_role | `to service_role ... using (true)` | `contacts_select_service` |\n\nNote on `update`: the task only requires \"no anon insert/update\" for books and none for the others, so no update policies are written — RLS denies all non-granted operations for anon.\n\n### 5. Additional considerations / potential issues\n1. **`updated_at` auto-update**: The books table has `updated_at` but no trigger to keep it fresh. Suggest an optional trigger, or note that admin updates should set it explicitly. Not required by the task, so left as an open decision.\n2. **`service_role` note for admin reads**: The admin portal (P1, stretch) will need the `service_role` key from Supabase Dashboard -> Settings -> API -> `service_role` secret. That key bypasses RLS. This is a deliberate design choice driven by RLS matching \"SELECT by service_role\". It works, but be aware the service_role key must be kept server-side/secret (not in `VITE_` env vars). The current front-end client `src/lib/supabase.js:3-4` uses only the anon key, so service_role reads will need separate wiring.\n3. **`to anon` vs `to public`**: For a Supabase app where signups aren't used, `anon` is the correct role (authenticated users are a separate role). Good.\n4. **`unique` on subscribers.email** matches SPEC \"TEXT UNIQUE\" (SPEC.md:245). Good.\n5. **`file_path`/`cover_image`** as TEXT mirrors SPEC's filepath fields and can hold Supabase storage public URLs or bucket paths. Consistent with SPEC.md:233-234.\n6. **`price` REAL default 0** matches the SPEC \"price (REAL, 0 for free)\" (SPEC.md:236).\n7. **Column ordering** — I kept the SPEC field order (SPEC.md:228-257) exactly as listed, satisfying \"ground the schema in the SPEC data model exactly\".\n\n### 6. Verification status\nReview mode — no files written, no build run. Since this is a standalone SQL file, no compile step is needed; correctness was verified against SPEC.md sections (lines 226-292) and the component/data requirements in PROGRESS.md (lines 241-245, 249-250).\n\n---\n\n**Open decisions for the lead:**\n- Add an `updated_at` trigger for `books`? (recommended: yes, small `set_updated_at` trigger function)\n- Confirm admin data access via `service_role` key (P1 admin portal), since the anon-key-only front-end cannot read subscribers/contacts.\n\nSince I'm in Review mode, I did not create the file. On approval I will write `supabase/schema.sql` with the exact content above."
