kground.svg\n10. .env.example with admin vars\n11. README-ish handoff? PROGRESS.md I shouldn't overwrite. I'll note in summary.\n\nLet me check if public/ dir exists. Earlier list showed no public/ folder. I'll create public/background.svg.\n\nLet me write the schema first.\n\nFor site_content table:\n- id uuid PK\n- section text unique (e.g. 'about', 'hero', 'offers')\n- content jsonb\n- updated_at\n\nBooks CRUD by anon demo policies. I'll add policies:\n- books: enable RLS, select published for anon (public site), AND an allow-all for anon to insert/update/delete for admin demo? That would leak. I'll create an `admin_role` concept? Can't without auth.\n\nLet me make a pragmatic choice: create separate policies granting anon insert/update/delete on books (demo), and anon select all (not just published) so admin dashboard can see drafts. Document clearly. Actually the Books component filters is_published=true client-side anyway, so anon select all + client filter. Fine.\n\nTo keep public API read of books having drafts is a slight leak but the client filter hides them. It's demo mode. OK.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nI'll write schema.sql now. Then books.js, admin.js. Then components. Then admin. Then App.jsx + index.css + background.svg + .env.example.\n\nLet me be efficient and write files confidently. I'll try to run npm install and build to verify.\n\nLet me start. I'll batch independent writes in parallel where possible (write_file calls are independent). But each write_file needs user approval; I'll issue them in a reasonable sequence. Let me do a few per message.\n\nFirst, update plan."
