      "report": "Review complete. I inspected the codebase read-only as required by my MODE. No files were modified.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Current state of the assigned column\n\nThe 6 components in my ownership do not exist yet — `src/components/` contains only `Logo.jsx` and `Reveal.jsx`. `src/App.jsx:1-9` imports all 9 sections already, so the build as-is would fail on module resolution. Each component needs to be created from scratch; everything needed to write them already exists.\n\n### 2. All tokens/copy needed are present — no gaps\n\n| Need | Source | Reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| `btn-gold`, `btn-ghost`, `eyebrow`, `gold-divider`, `container-x` | `src/index.css:39-57` | Ready to use directly in Tailwind classes |\n| `section[id]` anchor offset (88px) | `src/index.css:15-17` | Anchor jumps already offset for the fixed navbar |\n| `Logo` (default export) | `src/components/Logo.jsx:20` | `<Logo />` usable in navbar + footer |\n| `Reveal` (default, props `children/className/delay`) | `src/components/Reveal.jsx:7` | Wrap sections/items for fade-up |\n| `site` (name, owner, tagline, quote) | `src/lib/content.js:7-13` | Hero copy |\n| `about` (title, bio, portrait) | `src/lib/content.js:15-23` | About copy; note `portrait: null` — must render the null case gracefully |\n| `offers` (3 features with `icon` string) | `src/lib/content.js:25-49` | icon values: `book`, `gift`, `sparkles` |\n| `socials` | `src/lib/content.js:69-74` | Currently an **empty array** — footer must handle zero socials |\n| `lucide-react` | `package.json:14` | `book`, `gift`, `sparkles`, `chevron-down`, `menu`, `x` all available |\n| Theme colors | `tailwind.config.js:6-19` | `ink`, `charcoal`, `panel`, `gold`, `ivory`, `muted`, `line` |\n\n### 3. Concrete implementation plan / suggestions (for the build pass)\n\n**Navbar.jsx** — fixed 70px header (`h-[70px]` per SPEC 4), transparent over hero, switch to `bg-ink` + border/shadow when `window.scrollY > 10` (add/remove a class via `useEffect` scroll listener, or use a `scrolled` state). Left: `<Logo />`. Right (hidden on mobile): links `#about`, `#offers`, `#download`, `#books`, `#contact` with gold hover (`hover:text-gold`). Mobile: `menu`/`x` toggle + full-screen overlay of `bg-ink`. Imports from `lucide-react`: `menu`, `x` (and optionally `useEffect/useState` from react). No `#top` link needed — `Logo` already anchors to `#top`.\n\n**Hero.jsx** — `<section id=\"top\" className=\"relative flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-ink\">`; center column with `eyebrow` (\"JCROWN DIGITALS\" / wordmark), h1 serif quote from `site.quote`, welcome paragraph from `site.tagline`, and a `chevron-down` link to `#about` pinned at the bottom (`absolute bottom-8`). Use the `Logo` wordmark and/or `site.name`. Add a subtle gold radial/gradient overlay. `min-h-screen` already gives 100vh.\n\n**About.jsx** — `<section id=\"about\">` two-column on `md:` (40/60 split per SPEC 4): left portrait, right bio. Portrait: `about.portrait` is null, so render a fallback placeholder (e.g. a `panel` with the `CrownMark` or `Portrait` courtesy block) instead of a broken `img`. Use `gold-divider` vertically/gold capped divider between columns and an `eyebrow` + `font-display` title from `about.title`; map `about.bio` paragraphs.\n\n**Offers.jsx** — `<section id=\"offers\">` with `eyebrow` + `offers.title`/`offers.description`; `grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3` of feature cards. Each card: `bg-panel border border-line rounded` with hover lift + gold border glow — e.g. `transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-gold hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(201,168,76,0.15)]`. Icon: map `offers.features[i].icon` string → lucide component (`book`, `gift`, `sparkles`) in a small gold-dashed ring.\n\n**DownloadCTA.jsx** — `<section id=\"download\">` centered; a large gold button `btn-gold` with label **DOWNLOAD BOOKS HERE** (`<a href=\"#books\" className=\"btn-gold ...\">`). Keep `<a>` not `<button>` since it's an anchor (`#books`), or `btn-ghost` secondary link. Centered with generous `py-24/32`.\n\n**Footer.jsx** — `<footer className=\"bg-charcoal/40 border-t border-line\">`; brand `<Logo />` + `site.owner`, quick links to `#about/#offers/#books/#contact`, placeholder links \"Privacy Policy\" and \"Terms\" (SPEC 4 — likely `href=\"#\"` or `#top`), then `socials` from `content.js` — but `socials` is an **empty array**, so the footer must render nothing (or a fixed placeholder) for links rather than crashing; ` {new Date().getFullYear()} {site.name}`.\n\n### 4. Risks / edge cases to handle\n\n- `about.portrait` is null and `socials` is `[]` — both must render gracefully (no broken images, no empty link lists), or the implementer should add copy/placeholders in `content.js`.\n- `Navbar` scroll state — use a passive scroll listener and clean up in `useEffect` to avoid leaks; consider `prefers-reduced-motion` (already handled globally in CSS at `src/index.css:83-93`).\n- Specify `<a href=\"#books\">` for the CTA and `href=\"#about\"` for the hero chevron — the 88px scroll-margin in `index.css:16` handles offset.\n- No TypeScript, functional components only, default exports named to match the `App.jsx` imports (`Navbar`, `Hero`, `About`, `Offers`, `DownloadCTA`, `Footer`).\n\n### 5. Verification note\n\nI ran no commands (read-only mode). After building, verify with `npm install` (node_modules currently absent) then `npm run build`. All required dependencies (`react`, `lucide-react`) are already in `package.json:12-17`.\n\n**Decision taken:** the assigned task says \"build,\" but my MODE is Review — I did not create or modify files. I'm reporting the findings and a precise, ready-to-execute plan for the build pass.",
